  "caption": "Quinn sneezed and the side went zing. Twisting and deep breaths did too, and three weeks later the internet's “pulled muscle” theory wasn't holding up.\n\nKay explained that rib and side pain has many possible sources, including the mid-back joints, rib cartilage and the nerves between the ribs. Serious causes get ruled out first, then the plan.\n\nWhat can help: restoring mid-back extension and rotation, slow belly breathing, hugging a pillow when you cough or sneeze, and getting reassessed if there's no progress in four to eight weeks.\n\nGet checked promptly for chest pressure, breathlessness, one-sided chest pain, blood in urine, yellow skin, a fall or injury, fever, night pain, or a blistery rash.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
